   "note": "Proposed a highly expressive block with 12 trainable parameters. Structure: Layer 1 uses mixed rotations (RX, RY, RZ) on all qubits to break symmetry and introduce diverse basis changes. Layer 2 uses a cyclic CNOT chain (0-1-2-3-4-5-0) for global entanglement. Layer 3 applies RZ rotations to all qubits to adjust phases. Layer 4 repeats the cyclic CNOT chain to re-entangle after phase shifts. This 'brick-wall' style with cyclic connectivity ensures strong mixing across all sites, addressing the limitations of previous proposals that had lower gate counts or restricted connectivity. The high parameter count allows fitting complex non-linear relationships between the 6 inputs and 2 outputs.",
